[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7781"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+8y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+8{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +4)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =-4.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-64706/selection/431046250afbdc058224a8a1fce68aad3ef9dca7544ee81fd57eb775ca92ce1b" :answer/id #uuid "6dbb3384-88ba-545c-9acc-559b3912a797" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{3x}-3{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64706/selection/9795f04696e433cfa5eba8edb476b20ee000a5a6a8d5481b865b3f0adfd72505" :answer/id #uuid "831f0e6d-724e-516f-9e29-25f0172e95dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64706/selection/2ae5746a0b8e6710c744d0d2c4f899695120325a7b64c3896513fe419708a4db" :answer/id #uuid "395157eb-0911-5cc6-85be-7308cf221148" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{-x}+4{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64706/selection/5069f335b42796823d121fde4dd15c27f6f9c0257110b09c8226bb086d29ea7f" :answer/id #uuid "ba979d18-04bc-5dd9-846f-a5d37c06ed9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64706/selection/5d1c30ff84d54105513960269c95fff52eb65f04ec78d581704c6c2881b29a61" :answer/id #uuid "26d3360f-43e6-53d0-bd68-d037f76ae20f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64706/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b48aa4a7-b1fc-5bff-9c8a-c84ab1e6c7ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64706/selection/5069f335b42796823d121fde4dd15c27f6f9c0257110b09c8226bb086d29ea7f" :answer-field/choices ["q-64706/selection/431046250afbdc058224a8a1fce68aad3ef9dca7544ee81fd57eb775ca92ce1b" "q-64706/selection/9795f04696e433cfa5eba8edb476b20ee000a5a6a8d5481b865b3f0adfd72505" "q-64706/selection/2ae5746a0b8e6710c744d0d2c4f899695120325a7b64c3896513fe419708a4db" "q-64706/selection/5069f335b42796823d121fde4dd15c27f6f9c0257110b09c8226bb086d29ea7f" "q-64706/selection/5d1c30ff84d54105513960269c95fff52eb65f04ec78d581704c6c2881b29a61"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64706" :question/id #uuid "670e5717-fad8-5791-a10e-1498d79849c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-64706" :question/problem "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}-3y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-3{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -3)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =3.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-x}$ and ${e}^{3x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $-5{e}^{-3x}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64706/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcb5d818-acb0-53c7-90f9-328256600175"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64706"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64707"] :question/problem "Given that $y=y(t)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}-4y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}+3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}-4{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-4$ or $\\lambda =1.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-4t}$ and ${e}^{t}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $-{e}^{-4t}+{e}^{-t}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-90722/selection/9e7d1adff53537ff3f538f231519c47bc9fd0b0d95585f76d0d614cbe3a9f47b" :answer/id #uuid "a0ecf1d4-d1b0-5e0d-8f7d-9b31486c5c35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90722/selection/f66c112203f78e01d5887a960224165f85254d4cda6576e6a4fc33b84494d380" :answer/id #uuid "25916f0c-ecda-5e3b-9987-65b843b2c208" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90722/selection/a5e801fa60d3bd86032e76b1f0673972d4afe8a3aa16409b4f12d34b39feb166" :answer/id #uuid "63223857-37d1-541d-804a-9730f96f10ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{14x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90722/selection/674c2e345490001dea3387a17e237353d9c2e95d333376942771337444823814" :answer/id #uuid "8a0adeb8-9c4b-5724-92e0-ec3082fd6eb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-14x}+B{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90722/selection/a022d5b0e16b0cafa408534dbeabf811906ae4f70733d2799212135a456c7f34" :answer/id #uuid "92569b16-e86c-5066-9520-43a7f8ad905c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-7x}+B{e}^{-4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90722/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2325434b-54bf-56df-8473-6d06e13de0cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90722/selection/f66c112203f78e01d5887a960224165f85254d4cda6576e6a4fc33b84494d380" :answer-field/choices ["q-90722/selection/9e7d1adff53537ff3f538f231519c47bc9fd0b0d95585f76d0d614cbe3a9f47b" "q-90722/selection/f66c112203f78e01d5887a960224165f85254d4cda6576e6a4fc33b84494d380" "q-90722/selection/a5e801fa60d3bd86032e76b1f0673972d4afe8a3aa16409b4f12d34b39feb166" "q-90722/selection/674c2e345490001dea3387a17e237353d9c2e95d333376942771337444823814" "q-90722/selection/a022d5b0e16b0cafa408534dbeabf811906ae4f70733d2799212135a456c7f34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90722" :question/id #uuid "206538c4-544c-533a-b6a8-2e2938267cac" :question/math-academy-id "q-90722" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-11\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+28y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-11\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+28{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-11\\lambda +28) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-11\\lambda +28=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -7)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =4$ or $\\lambda =7.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{7x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-90722/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe7e5c4f-6ac0-58e8-8b95-fe5a2230341c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90722"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130118/selection/eb28e6eea8f0554797839e7f0c9c9062764679da850519289f679a958bec7cdd" :answer/id #uuid "95106564-a137-582a-b583-d1be407d85f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130118/selection/e9bde627131f1294353199b927063e7da268c25479d91edafe58085ae68c0f75" :answer/id #uuid "03b8a4eb-5926-5b39-838c-eb42edb068fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130118/selection/fc28e03b24ceb5065406fedb874ab985590a6df8a4cecb88b1cf608ab50a1e61" :answer/id #uuid "0e0556aa-9b10-5ae0-8448-b3a93b10d052" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130118/selection/ec7a35df67208469164d9218b433916c2fe5a05dc57fe1d0f392fdac7940016e" :answer/id #uuid "866058ed-b3a2-5418-ac4f-ca1999de2e8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130118/selection/0bd36910c8ca77e11ad83577032f8eddb8111a11df81729e2be51320384fc717" :answer/id #uuid "dd0e14a7-1831-52de-b97d-f9bbca01cb51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130118/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3fb6eb3-577e-5782-86b5-8fbd4c870479" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130118/selection/ec7a35df67208469164d9218b433916c2fe5a05dc57fe1d0f392fdac7940016e" :answer-field/choices ["q-130118/selection/eb28e6eea8f0554797839e7f0c9c9062764679da850519289f679a958bec7cdd" "q-130118/selection/e9bde627131f1294353199b927063e7da268c25479d91edafe58085ae68c0f75" "q-130118/selection/fc28e03b24ceb5065406fedb874ab985590a6df8a4cecb88b1cf608ab50a1e61" "q-130118/selection/ec7a35df67208469164d9218b433916c2fe5a05dc57fe1d0f392fdac7940016e" "q-130118/selection/0bd36910c8ca77e11ad83577032f8eddb8111a11df81729e2be51320384fc717"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130118" :question/id #uuid "423c3716-190e-5b6f-9635-03a5ec2b0925" :question/math-academy-id "q-130118" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-5\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+4{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +4=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =1$ or $\\lambda =4.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{4x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130118/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe7e5c4f-6ac0-58e8-8b95-fe5a2230341c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130118"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
